Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Traced every previously-unclassified worker's real config fields against
actual server code (server files, the setup wizard, each hinges panel) —
same rigor pin-down/rep-onboarding already established, not guessed:

- pre-call-read: 17 real fields classified (brief destination, video
  engagement tracking + credential, prospect research sources + Apollo/PDL
  credentials, call-intelligence provider + Recall credential/region/bot
  name, plus 4 fields confirmed real but currently unbuilt — no UI setter
  exists anywhere for them yet, flagged honestly rather than omitted).
- leak-map: 8 fields (report format/destination, schedules, timezone,
  existing-audit/notification-pack flags collected on pin-down's own
  setup screen on Leak Map's behalf, plus one unbuilt field).
- pile-on: 7 fields (SMS platform + credential + compliance status/footer,
  ad-data platform + credential, existing-sequence flag). Confirmed no
  credential of its own beyond these — resolveCredential is keyed by
  engagementId + provider, so it draws from the exact same rows pin-down's
  onboarding already wrote for anything it shares.
- win-back: 6 fields (reschedule mode, no-show tagging, inbound-reply
  mode + HubSpot portal id, plus 2 unbuilt cadence fields).
- rep-engine-panel, rep-trustpilot-watch, rep-reddit-watch,
  rep-twitter-watch, rep-crisis-response: verified to need NOTHING beyond
  rep-onboarding's repIdentityGraphs fields — every API key each one uses
  is a global platform credential (OUTSCRAPER_API_KEY, REDDITAPIS_API_KEY,
  TWITTERAPIS_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, the REP_ENGINE_MODEL_* vars),
  not a per-client secret. Confirmed empty, not just unclassified — the
  WorkerDefinition doc comment now documents this distinction directly.

Also fixed a real gap this verification pass surfaced: rep-onboarding's
own classified list was missing 3 fields (entities, seedPanelPrompts,
activeEngines) that identity-graph-form.tsx actually collects and that
rep-engine-panel/rep-reddit-watch/rep-twitter-watch genuinely depend on —
their "needs nothing new" verdict above is only true with these included.

Lighter-form fallback: pile-on is the one worker with real ask-kind fields
and no hinges panel to answer them in (every other classified worker
already has hasHingesPanel: true, a real dedicated setup page). Added
EnablePileOnModal — two grouped dropdowns (SMS platform, ad-data platform),
both optional, persisted through the existing, deliberately-scoped PATCH
/api/engagements/[id] route (confirmed both fields are already in its
explicit allowlist, not a new arbitrary-merge risk). "Skip for now"
preserves today's blind-enable behavior as an escape hatch. Deliberately
NOT generalized into a registry-driven form for every worker yet — most
of the other 6 newly-classified fields aren't in that route's allowlist,
and a fragile generic abstraction over an explicitly-scoped security
boundary is worse than a correct, narrow one. Generalizing is a real next
step once a second worker needs the same treatment.

